---
description: Keep the quote path from hanging or firing twice.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Quote path

## Now

- Time out the vendor call in the BFF. A slow vendor must not pile up requests.
- Disable Generate Quote while a request is in flight so a double click does not call the vendor again. The web rule covers how that loading state looks.

## Leave out

Retries wait until the vendor agrees a repeat call is safe. The same loan details can return a new `quoteId` today.

## Load test target

One Gatling TypeScript simulation in `load/` (`pnpm load`). It is not part of `pnpm test`. It calls the BFF only, once per user, with no retry. The mock vendor still answers each call. Set `VENDOR_FAILURE_RATE` to 0 so a random fake error is not counted as a capacity problem. 50 users at once. Most calls under a few seconds. No crash. No leaked key. Watch timeout piles. The Gatling CLI wants Node.js 24.

## Example

```ts
// BAD: the vendor call can hang forever
await fetch(vendorUrl, { method: "POST", body });

// GOOD: give up after a fixed time
await fetch(vendorUrl, {
  method: "POST",
  body,
  signal: AbortSignal.timeout(Number(process.env.VENDOR_TIMEOUT_MS)),
});
```
